    <statement><p>Consider the function <m>f(x)</m> graphed below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap2Sec5__Q01_pg-image-1.png" width="50%"/>
<p>For this function, are the following nonzero quantities positive or
negative?</p>
<p><m>f(4)</m> is <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><m>f'(4)</m> is <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0002"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><m>f''(4)</m> is <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0003"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><em>(Because this is a multiple choice problem, it will not
show which parts of the problem are correct or incorrect when you
submit it.)</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{positive}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{negative}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{negative}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x</m>-axis at <m>x=4</m>,
the value of <m>f(4)</m> is positive.




Since <m>f(x)</m> is decreasing at <m>x = 4</m>,
the value of <m>f'(4)</m> is negative.




Since <m>f(x)</m> is concave down at <m>x = 4</m>, 
the value of <m>f''(4)</m> is negative.



</solution>
